From: Gleb Pesin <dormancygrace@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 17:00:24 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 10/16] riscv: switch XTheadVector state before restoring the
 next FCSR

On the C906 (XTheadVector) the vector fixed-point fields VXRM and VXSAT are
part of FCSR. __switch_to_fpu() loads the next task's FCSR, so a vector
switch after it would save the previous task's vxrm/vxsat from the next
task's FCSR. Switch the vector state first on XTheadVector cores; other
cores keep the upstream order.

[Adapted to 6.18: no srmcfg switch.]
---
 arch/riscv/include/asm/switch_to.h | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/riscv/include/asm/switch_to.h b/arch/riscv/include/asm/switch_to.h
index 0e71eb82f..dd50fa3b3 100644
--- a/arch/riscv/include/asm/switch_to.h
+++ b/arch/riscv/include/asm/switch_to.h
@@ -115,9 +115,12 @@ do {							\
 	struct task_struct *__prev = (prev);		\
 	struct task_struct *__next = (next);		\
 	__set_prev_cpu(__prev->thread);			\
+	/* C906 FCSR aliases VXRM/VXSAT: save V before restoring next FCSR. */ \
+	if (has_xtheadvector())				\
+		__switch_to_vector(__prev, __next);	\
 	if (has_fpu())					\
 		__switch_to_fpu(__prev, __next);	\
-	if (has_vector() || has_xtheadvector())		\
+	if (has_vector() && !has_xtheadvector())		\
 		__switch_to_vector(__prev, __next);	\
 	if (switch_to_should_flush_icache(__next))	\
 		local_flush_icache_all();		\
